  "answer": "Assuming NY Medicaid: the documents give no copay tier for Trulicity. NYRx uses PDL preferred/non-preferred status, not tiers.\n\n- Trulicity® is **preferred** on the NYRx PDL in the GLP-1 RA (Type 2 diabetes) class. The row carries no flags, and no effective-date marker applies.\n- Class CC applies: confirm an FDA-approved or compendia-supported indication that Medicaid covers.\n- PA is required if the patient is also on a DPP-4 inhibitor.\n\nThe Part D documents here cover opioid policy only, not formulary tiers. If the patient has Part D, check the plan's formulary. The VA guidance doesn't give tiers either.",
